# Dev folders (NEVER PUBLISH - development artifacts only)
# Wildcard pattern catches all: docs_dev, scripts_dev, tests_dev, samples_dev,
# examples_dev, downloads_dev, libs_dev, builds_dev, etc.
*_dev/

# Claude Code local state — everything EXCEPT the shared PROJECT memory corpus.
#
# `.claude/*` (glob), not `.claude/` (bare directory). This is load-bearing: git
# does not descend into an excluded DIRECTORY, so under the bare form every
# `!.claude/...` negation below would be INERT. Verified empirically 2026-07-29
# in a throwaway repo — `.claude/` + negations tracks nothing, `.claude/*` +
# `!.claude/project/` tracks the memory files.
#
# The negations re-include ONE path and nothing else. Everything private stays
# ignored by construction: chat_history/ (conversation exports), settings.local.json,
# cache/, scheduled_tasks*, .janitor/, worktrees/, .DS_Store.
#
# Why this is now safe for the CPV release gate (it was not, before 2026-08-07):
# CPV's `.claude/` check became CONTENT-AWARE in its issue #120 —
# `validate_plugin._claude_dir_has_tracked_content()`, asserted by
# `tests/test_issue_120_claude_dir_gitignore.py::test_tracked_claude_content_clears_finding`
# on a fixture using exactly this glob+negation shape. Separately the
# required-entries audit (`standardize_plugin._gitignore_line_covers_entry`) accepts
# any glob that fnmatch-covers `.claude/` — running CPV's own predicate, `.claude/*`
# returns True — and it emits WARN, not MINOR. PSS gates via `uvx --from git+https://…`,
# i.e. CPV main, so the fix is in the gating version. Confirmed end-to-end on
# 2026-08-07: `cpv-remote-validate plugin .` → CRITICAL=0 MAJOR=0 MINOR=0, no
# `.claude/` finding at all.
#
# The finding clears on TRACKED CONTENT, so this spelling and the committed memory
# files must land TOGETHER — changing one without the other re-opens the finding.
.claude/*
!.claude/project/
# ...but NOT the janitor's generated detector proposals. These are regenerated on
# every scan and deleted once the finding clears, so tracking one means a deleted-
# then-recreated file in every contributor's status forever. They are artifacts,
# not knowledge — the knowledge lands in a real memory page.
.claude/project/memory/*-proposed.md
CLAUDE.md

# ai-maestro-janitor runtime state (logs + timestamps; regenerated on every fire)
.janitor/

# TLDR CLI cache
.tldr/
.tldrignore

# Environment files
.env
.env.*

# Virtual environments
.venv/

# Testing cache
.pytest_cache/

# Node
node_modules/

# Rust build artifacts (covers both main repo and submodule)
target/

# bin/ is TRACKED — contains pre-built PSS binaries for all platforms
# (binaries moved from src/skill-suggester/bin/ to top-level bin/ in v2.5.0)

# Agent & LLM-tool report output — ALL gitignored because reports often contain
# private data (paths, tokens, prompts, redacted-but-still-sensitive snippets).
# Per the global rule: agents must always save their reports under ./reports/
# in the project root, even when running inside a separate worktree.
# ./reports_dev/ is the local archive for rotated-out old reports; also gitignored
# (*_dev/ wildcard above catches it, listed explicitly here for clarity).
/reports/
/reports_dev/
llm_externalizer_output/

# Deprecated files (moved to *_dev/ folders)
# pss_release.py → scripts_dev/ (superseded by pss_ship.py)
# requirements.txt → docs_dev/ (superseded by pyproject.toml + uv)
.rechecker/
# TLDR artifacts (added by rechecker)
.tldr_session_*

rck-*-merge-pending.md

# Added by CPV standardize
.coverage
/.trashcan/*
!/.trashcan/.gitkeep
!/.trashcan/README.txt
# (This block used to hold three `!.claude/project/memory/...` negations plus a
# comment asserting they had been REMOVED as inert. Both halves were wrong at
# once: the lines were still present, and once the entry above became `.claude/*`
# they stopped being inert and started WINNING — gitignore is last-match-wins, so
# being further down the file they silently overrode the `*-proposed.md` exclusion
# up there. Removed 2026-08-08. The single `!.claude/project/` negation at that
# entry is sufficient and is the only place this is decided; do not re-add
# per-entry negations here, and do not trust a comment that claims a line is gone
# without looking for it.)
